body:
This doc comment and the inline comment at lines 134-135 both describe the pre-PR per-app cache path (OTELC_TEST_GOCACHE/<app>). The code below now points GOCACHE directly at the shared cacheRoot, so builds across different apps — and different instrumentation configs — share one cache. Go's build cache is content-addressed so this should be safe, but both comments need updating to match: the inline one currently says "reuse this app-local cache without sharing compiled objects across different instrumentation configs," which asserts the opposite of what the code now does.

```suggestion
// Build builds the application with the instrumentation tool. The built binary
// is registered for cleanup via t.Cleanup. Standard test apps use
// OTELC_TEST_GOCACHE as a shared GOCACHE when OTELC_TEST_GOCACHE is set, and
// drop -a so warm builds can reuse that shared cache. Custom appsDir builds
// keep the caller's arguments and environment unchanged.
```

