body:
The walk-up has no bound besides the filesystem root. In practice the
three-go.mod fingerprint (root + pkg/go.mod + instrumentation/go.mod) is
specific enough that a false-positive match is unlikely, but a short
comment would make the intentional lack of a stopping condition clear to
future readers instead of looking like an oversight.

```suggestion
	// No depth limit beyond the filesystem root: the combination of a root
	// go.mod plus pkg/go.mod and instrumentation/go.mod nested under it is
	// specific enough that false positives are not expected in practice.
	for {
		if util.PathExists(filepath.Join(root, "go.mod")) &&
			util.PathExists(filepath.Join(root, "pkg", "go.mod")) &&
			util.PathExists(filepath.Join(root, "instrumentation", "go.mod")) {
			return root, nil
		}
		parent := filepath.Dir(root)
		if parent == root {
			break
		}
		root = parent
	}
