body:
Worth making this explicit in the doc: unaliased `.vN`-suffixed last segments
(e.g. `example.com/pkg.v2`) are now stripped unconditionally, not just under
`gopkg.in/`. The pre-unification `instrument.defaultImportAlias` only stripped
`.vN` when the path started with `gopkg.in/`; this merge adopts `ast`'s broader
rule for both call sites. That's a deliberate (and narrow) behavior change for
`instrument`'s matching — worth a one-line note so a future reader doesn't
mistake it for an oversight.

```suggestion
// packages are matched only when the importing file aliases them explicitly.
//
// Note: the ".vN" strip applies to any path whose last segment looks like a
// version (not only gopkg.in/ paths) — this is intentionally broader than the
// instrument package's pre-unification helper, to keep both callers consistent.
```

